# Install Syncthing on Windows

This plan outlines the steps to install Syncthing on Windows using the `winget` package manager. We will install **SyncTrayzor**, which provides a graphical user interface and system tray integration for a better experience on Windows.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be installing **SyncTrayzor (GermanCoding.SyncTrayzor)**, which is a GUI wrapper for Syncthing. If you prefer the command-line version only, please let me know.

## Proposed Changes

### Installation

- Run `winget install --id GermanCoding.SyncTrayzor` to install the application.
- This will install both Syncthing and the SyncTrayzor GUI.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will check if the SyncTrayzor executable exists in the standard installation path.
- I will attempt to run `syncthing --version` if possible to verify the core engine.

### Manual Verification
- The user can open SyncTrayzor from the Start menu and access the Web UI (usually at `http://127.0.0.1:8384`).
